# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LLM "brain" configuration (OPTIONAL).
#
# Leave ALL of these blank/unset to run in MOCK MODE — the app fully works with
# rule-based answers built from products.json. Zero key, zero cost, zero signup.
#
# To upgrade to a real LLM, copy this file to `.env` and fill in a FREE-TIER
# OpenAI-compatible provider. The values below are commented examples — pick ONE.
# `.env` is git-ignored so your key never gets committed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Option A: Groq (free tier, very fast) — https://console.groq.com/keys ──────
# VITE_LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# VITE_LLM_API_KEY=gsk_your_free_key_here
# VITE_LLM_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile

# ── Option B: OpenRouter (has free models) — https://openrouter.ai/keys ────────
# VITE_LLM_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# VITE_LLM_API_KEY=sk-or-your_free_key_here
# VITE_LLM_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct:free

# ── Option C: Google Gemini (free tier, OpenAI-compatible endpoint) ────────────
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# VITE_LLM_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai
# VITE_LLM_API_KEY=your_free_gemini_key_here
# VITE_LLM_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash

# ── Option D: Self-hosted / local (Ollama, LM Studio, llama.cpp) — $0 forever ──
# VITE_LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# VITE_LLM_API_KEY=ollama
# VITE_LLM_MODEL=llama3.2
